Z||000000||samsgirl||11-18-1999||02:46 PM||||<BR>Hi Ladies and Gents,<BR>I just bought my first Fiero last weekend - an 86 SE that has seen some better days.<P>When I test drove it, I could not get it into 1st gear, but the owner was selling it under the premise that it needed a new clutch, so I figured it would get better after the clutch went in.<P>I got the car back after my very trustworthy repair shop put the new clutch in.  I still can't get it into 1st.  I called the old owner, and he said that it has been like that since he bought it brand new.  That explains why it needed a new clutch with only 55,000 on the odometer - it has taken off in 2nd its whole life.  Is this normal for Fieros?  Is there a way to fix it?  I am going to drive this car in the winter, and I want to be able to downshift if I'm on ice.  Thanks in advance for any input!  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||88 Fiero||11-18-1999||02:59 PM||||First check and see if your clutch pedal has been replace with a steel type...The clutch that came with the factory is aluminum and can cause to bend and will not shift to gears properly... Second see if your Master Cylinder is not leaking....I think you still have the aluminum clutch pedal in which you need to replace it with a steel type...either way check it...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||11-18-1999||03:25 PM||||Also check the linkage adjustment. Can you easily shift through all the gears if the car is not running?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||11-18-1999||03:31 PM||||After finally giving up on my clutch, I picked up a slave cylinder last night and while tinkering, I found that the pedal is the screwed up aluminum one. I will order a steel one on the way home today. It is a good thing that I really like this car!||||reg||1
Z||000004||ggarsk||11-18-1999||07:55 PM||||Cooter,when you pick up your new clutch pedal don't forget to get pedal shaft bushings. It will save you a trip to the parts store later.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||11-18-1999||08:03 PM||||I had an 86SE V6 with the 4 speed that always had to be forced into 1st and would grind going in reverse (had to kill the motor and start after shifting to revese). I bled and bled and swore and finally got advise to replace the pedal. I did and the thing shited like a dream (not as slick as my 88 5spd though). The pedal didn't appear to be bent but it was....||||reg||1
Z||000006||Terrybogin||11-18-1999||08:44 PM||||I hate it when my car shited.||||reg||10
Z||000007||Patrick||11-18-1999||09:16 PM||||<BR>That's usually what my passenger's done when I've cornered too fast...||||reg||12
Z||000008||CUTTER||11-18-1999||10:10 PM||||LOL||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||11-18-1999||11:31 PM||||If the pedal was bent, why would it go into second gear ok, but not first? Those aluminum pedals are a problem, I know, I have to replace the one on my 85 GT, it's really twisted up after that last race I had with a Honda CRX SI. However, it also could be a bent shifter fork in the tranny, or like was said earlier, the shifter linkage adjustment. If the pedal looked ok, I'd check the adjustment first.<P>It's nice to get another lady on the Forum, welcome! At least with that nickname, I'm assuming you're female. But, you've already broke my heart announcing you're someone else's girl. **hanging head in disappointment**||||reg||1
Z||000010||batboy||11-18-1999||11:35 PM||||Woo hoo! I just now checked Samsgirl's profile. Sam is her horse! **Straining to see if her left hand has a ring**  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Just joking Samsgirl. Again welcome, hope you can get your cool little Fiero up and running real soon without it being something too expensive!<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 11-19-1999).]||||reg||12
Z||000011||Patrick||11-19-1999||01:21 AM||||<BR>I see that poor <B>Sam</B> is also a <B>gelding</B>. I may be a city boy, but even I know what that means. Ooooo, it gives me the willies just thinking about it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>Hello <B>samsgirl</B>, don't take us too seriously. This is just our way of welcoming you to the forum. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000012||ChadMan||11-19-1999||09:51 AM||||Hey samsgirl, does your SE shift smoothly into 3rd?  Your 1st gear problem could be caused by a shifter cable, but if it were, you would probably notice some difficulty shifting into 3rd too.  Just my 2 cents.<BR>||||reg||1
